        "id": "A11Y-16",
        "priority": "low",
        "criterion": "WCAG 1.4.3 — exempt, recorded as advisory",
        "screen": "styles.css:218–221 — .btn.primary:disabled",
        "observation": "Disabled buttons are rendered at `opacity: 0.5`, giving the 'Not enough' state a computed 3.96:1 text contrast. WCAG explicitly exempts inactive user-interface components from 1.4.3, so this is not a failure. It is recorded because 'Not enough' is a disabled control that carries information the member needs, and at 3.96:1 on a phone in a bright clubhouse it is information the 60+ cohort may not be able to read.",
        "fix": "Do not use opacity to express disabled state on controls that carry meaning. Use a distinct, readable disabled token, and move the information out of the button label (see heuristic 2).",
        "confidence": "validated"
      }
    ],

    "needsVerification": [
      {
        "id": "A11Y-V1",
        "criterion": "WCAG 2.4.11 Focus Not Obscured (Minimum) (Level AA) — new in WCAG 2.2",
        "observation": "The tab bar is `position: fixed; bottom: 0` with `padding: 8px 8px calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))` (styles.css:92–104), and .content reserves 96px (styles.css:65). Computed bar height is roughly 67px before the safe-area inset; on a notched iOS device the inset is ~34px, giving ~101px — more than the 96px reserved. The last focusable element on a fully scrolled page could therefore be partially obscured on those devices.",
        "howToVerify": "Tab to the last control on a long History list on a notched device and confirm the focus ring is fully visible.",
        "fix": "Compute the reservation from the same expression: `padding-bottom: calc(96px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))`."
      },
      {
        "id": "A11Y-V2",
        "criterion": "WCAG 2.4.7 Focus Visible (Level AA) — user-agent default rings",
        "observation": "Buttons, links and tabs have no authored focus style and depend on the browser's default ring rendering over a very dark background (--bg #0b1020). Chrome's default ring is two-tone and generally survives dark backgrounds; older WebKit and some Android WebViews do not render as reliably.",
        "howToVerify": "Keyboard-traverse each route in Safari/iOS, Chrome/Android and desktop Chrome and Firefox.",
        "fix": "Author the focus style explicitly rather than relying on the default (see A11Y-11)."
      },
      {
        "id": "A11Y-V3",
        "criterion": "WCAG 1.4.10 Reflow (AA) / 1.4.4 Resize Text (AA)",
        "observation": "See A11Y-14. Overflow at 320px / 200% is computed, not observed.",
        "howToVerify": "320px viewport at 200% text zoom, and iOS Dynamic Type at the largest accessibility size on the installed PWA.",
        "fix": "As A11Y-14."
      },
      {
        "id": "A11Y-V4",
        "criterion": "Offline behaviour — supports NFR-007 / NFR-009 and RAID R010",
        "observation": "vite.config.ts:33–42 caches /api NetworkFirst with a 5s timeout and a 5-minute expiry. What a member sees at a till with no connectivity — a stale balance, a spinner, or a raw 'Failed to fetch' — has not been observed. This is a member-safety question, not only an accessibility one.",
        "howToVerify": "Throttle to offline and to 2G on each route, cold and warm start.",
        "fix": "Specify the offline contract for the card and balance explicitly before RA-06."
      }
    ],

    "contrastResults": {
      "note": "Computed 2026-08-17 from styles.css declared values using the WCAG relative-luminance formula. Alpha layers composited against their actual backdrop; the points-card gradient (linear-gradient 135deg, #4f46e5 → #7c3aed) is evaluated at its midpoint #6640e9 and at both endpoints. Requirement column: 4.5 = 1.4.3 normal text; 3.0 = 1.4.11 non-text.",
      "textPairs": [
        { "pair": "--text #eef1f8 on --bg #0b1020 (body)", "ratio": "16.74:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--text on --surface #151b30 (.card, .list-item, .stat)", "ratio": "15.08:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--text on --surface-2 #1d2540 (input value, .btn, .toast)", "ratio": "13.35:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--muted #94a0be on --bg (.muted, .small 13.1px)", "ratio": "7.24:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--muted on --surface (list date, stat label, form label)", "ratio": "6.52:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--muted on --surface-2 (inactive segmented button)", "ratio": "5.77:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--muted on tab bar (inactive tab, 11.5px)", "ratio": "6.59:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--text on tab bar (active tab, 11.5px)", "ratio": "15.24:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--primary #6366f1 on --bg (.link 'See all', 13.6px)", "ratio": "4.24:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "FAIL — A11Y-07" },
        { "pair": "--primary on --surface (.cost 'N pts', 16px bold)", "ratio": "3.82:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "FAIL — A11Y-07" },
        { "pair": "--neg #f87171 on --bg (.error 14.4px)", "ratio": "6.84:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--neg on --surface (.delta.neg)", "ratio": "6.17:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "--pos #34d399 on --surface (.delta.pos)", "ratio": "8.87:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "#fff on --primary-strong #4f46e5 (.btn.primary, active segment)", "ratio": "6.29:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "#fff on points-card gradient midpoint #6640e9", "ratio": "6.04:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "#fff on gradient end #7c3aed (worst point)", "ratio": "5.70:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "rgba(255,255,255,0.85) on gradient mid (.points-label, .tier-row .muted, 13.6px)", "ratio": "4.81:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "PASS — narrow margin" },
        { "pair": "#fff on .tier-badge fill (rgba(255,255,255,0.2) over gradient = #8566ed)", "ratio": "4.10:1", "required": "4.5:1", "result": "FAIL — A11Y-07" },
        { "pair": "Disabled .btn.primary at opacity 0.5 ('Not enough')", "ratio": "3.96:1", "required": "exempt", "result": "EXEMPT — advisory, A11Y-16" }
      ],
      "nonTextPairs": [
        { "pair": "input:focus border --primary vs --surface-2 (focus indicator)", "ratio": "3.38:1", "required": "3:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "input:focus border --primary vs --bg", "ratio": "4.24:1", "required": "3:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": ".toast border --primary vs --surface-2", "ratio": "3.38:1", "required": "3:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "progress fill #fff vs track #8c70ee", "ratio": "3.71:1", "required": "3:1", "result": "PASS" },
        { "pair": "input fill --surface-2 vs card --surface (component boundary)", "ratio": "1.13:1", "required": "3:1", "result": "FAIL — A11Y-08" },
        { "pair": "progress track #8c70ee vs points-card gradient mid", "ratio": "1.63:1", "required": "3:1", "result": "FAIL — A11Y-08" },
        { "pair": "--surface card vs --bg page", "ratio": "1.11:1", "required": "n/a", "result": "INFORMATIONAL — cards are not user-interface components, so 1.4.11 does not apply; recorded because the surface hierarchy is near-invisible and rests entirely on radius and shadowless separation" },
        { "pair": "tab-bar top border rgba(255,255,255,0.06)", "ratio": "1.18:1", "required": "n/a", "result": "INFORMATIONAL — decorative separator, not a boundary needed to identify a control" }
      ]
    },

    "seniorCohortNotes": {
      "context": "RA-08 recruits at least four participants aged 60+ and the brief names the Silvers sub-segment as the group most exposed by a SingPass-first, installable-PWA model. These are the current codebase's specific liabilities for that cohort, in priority order. None of them is exotic — they are all cheap to fix now and expensive to retrofit across twelve features.",
      "items": [
        "No autofill (A11Y-04). Typing an email and a password on a phone is the single highest-abandonment step, and the app has disabled the one mechanism that removes it.",
        "Small touch targets on the money controls (A11Y-12). 'Redeem' at ~32px and 'See all' at ~16px, against a 44pt/48dp platform expectation.",
        "Small type at the bottom of the size scale. The tab labels are 0.72rem (~11.5px) and .small is 0.82rem (~13.1px), used for transaction dates and stat labels. Contrast passes; legibility at 11.5px does not follow from that.",
        "A dark-only interface with no light mode and no prefers-color-scheme handling. Ageing eyes generally read dark-on-light more comfortably, and — decisively — the membership QR will need a light field to scan (see absentComponentRequirements).",
        "No help route and no support contact (heuristic 10). The cohort most likely to need CX has no way to reach it.",
        "Errors written in machine English ('Failed to fetch') with no recovery action (heuristic 9)."
      ]
    },

    "absentComponentRequirements": {
      "note": "The digital membership card (brief f1) does not exist and therefore cannot be audited. These are forward-looking requirements for the component when it is built, not findings against the current code. They are recorded here because the card is the single most accessibility-critical element in the product and because one of them — the light-field requirement — directly constrains the palette decision RA-09 has to make.",
      "requirements": [
        "The QR/barcode is non-text content encoding the member's identity: role=\"img\" with an accessible name, and the membership number rendered as real, selectable text beneath it. A member with a cracked screen, a screen-reader user, or anyone facing a scanner that will not read can then read the number aloud. Never make the visual code the only representation. (1.1.1)",
        "SCANNER CONSTRAINT — the code needs dark modules on a light field with a quiet zone of at least four modules. The app's only defined visual identity is dark-first (--bg #0b1020). A dark-mode QR is not reliably decodable by many POS scanners or by camera apps without inversion support. Either the card view breaks the theme with a light panel, or the programme is not dark-first. This is a design-system decision, not an implementation detail, and it belongs in RA-09.",
        "The card view should raise screen brightness (or explicitly prompt the member to), because auto-brightness in a dim F&B interior produces an unscannable screen. Restore the previous brightness on exit.",
        "Reachable in one action from a cold start and renderable with no network round-trip (brief guiding principle 1, NFR-009). Make this a measured acceptance criterion in RA-08, not an aspiration.",
        "If the card is presented in an overlay: trap focus within it, provide a visible and keyboard-reachable dismiss, and never dismiss it on a timer — a member at a counter may need longer than expected (2.2.1).",
        "State the card's freshness. If it renders from cache while offline, say so on the card rather than presenting stale data as live.",
        "Do not require a gesture (pinch, swipe, long-press) to reveal or enlarge the code without a single-pointer alternative (2.5.1)."
      ]
    }
  }
}
